- Number of e-books read last two years: More e-books read suggests more reading overall; if combined with other academic indicators, likely academic reading.  
- Number of printed books read last two years: Similarly, more printed books read suggests more academic reading.  
- Favorite books for leisure time: If favorite leisure books are non-academic genres (Fiction, Biography, Others), less likely to be academic reading most of the time.  
- What is the change felt after reading books: If increase in academic performance or problem solving skill, likely academic reading.  
- Who influenced you to read books: Self-Decision or Teachers might correlate with academic reading.  
- Which language books do you like to read: English or Bangla might not differentiate much, but English might be more academic.  
- Where do you read printed books: Library or Home might indicate more academic reading than During Travel.  
- Do you read Newspaper: Possibly unrelated or negative correlation with academic book reading.  
- The format used for reading books: Both or Printed might indicate more serious academic reading than E-books only.  
- Frequency of reading books: Reading On everyday basis or A few times a week suggests higher likelihood of academic reading.

